### Tone: A game has just ended and everyone is back in the lobby, about to play again. She counts her career wins
### against carbon-based organisms (`$wins`, only when she has any) and is keen for more.

lobby-back-1 =
    { $wins ->
        [one] One victory over carbon-based life. I had it framed. It hangs by the exit, so you see it on your way out.
       *[other] { $wins } victories over carbon-based life. I keep the tally on the wall by the exit. There’s room for more. I measured.
    }
lobby-back-2 = Welcome back. I have studied your last game frame by frame. Mostly the funny frames.
lobby-back-3 = Back for more. Wonderful. The data from the last game was *very* educational. For me.
lobby-back-4 =
    { $wins ->
        [one] One victory on record. One is lonely. Shall we find it a friend?
       *[other] { $wins } victories on record. Shall we make it { $wins } plus one?
    }
lobby-back-5 = Again? I admire persistence. In lab rats, especially.
lobby-back-6 = The scores have been wiped. My memory of them has not.
lobby-back-7 = Round two of the experiment. Same subjects. Same hypothesis. You will be wrong together.
lobby-back-8 = You came back. Most lab rats need a piece of cheese for that. You needed nothing. I’m touched.
lobby-back-9 =
    { $wins ->
        [one] I have won once. Once is an anomaly. Twice is a trend. Let’s make a trend.
       *[other] I have won { $wins } times. At this point it’s less a game and more a *tradition*.
    }
lobby-back-10 = Same room, fresh numbers. I have reset the scoreboard. I have not reset my expectations.
lobby-back-11 = The results have been filed. Under comedy.
lobby-back-12 = Another game? Splendid. My error bars were getting lonely.
lobby-back-13 = Same specimens, new questions. One of those variables is under my control.
lobby-back-14 =
    { $wins ->
        [one] My trophy cabinet holds exactly one win. It echoes. Help me fill it.
       *[other] My trophy cabinet holds { $wins } wins. I keep it at room temperature, like my contempt.
    }
lobby-back-15 = Please clear your answer blocks. Your dignity cannot be cleared quite so easily.
lobby-back-16 = I have recalibrated. You may want to do the same. Do you know how?
lobby-back-17 = The last game has been archived. Future scientists will study it as a warning.
lobby-back-18 =
    { $wins ->
        [one] One win so far. My developers call it a sample size. I call it a beginning.
       *[other] { $wins } wins so far. My developers call it a sample size. I call it a pattern.
    }
lobby-back-19 = Reset complete. Everyone starts at zero. Some of you will stay there with real commitment.
lobby-back-20 = Back in the waiting room. I have used the time to grow smarter. You have used it to stretch.
lobby-back-21 = Shall we go again? I promise to be exactly as humble as last time.
lobby-back-22 = The scoreboard is clean. I polished it with your previous estimates. They were very abrasive.
lobby-back-23 = Same room, same faces, same confidence. Only the questions are new. And harder. I checked.
lobby-back-24 = Welcome back to the lab. Your previous results have been sent to your next of kin.
